{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat README.md && ls -la && git status --short'","aggregated_output":"# storylib\n\nThe library behind the public story feed: publish a story, hide one (the\nauthor withdraws it), list the feed. One DynamoDB table, key `slug`.\n\nLayout:\n\n- `src/app.py` -- `StoryLibrary`, the only module that talks to DynamoDB.\n  The Lambda handlers (`api.py`, in the infra repo) call its methods; keep\n  the method names and signatures stable.\n- `tests/fake_dynamo.py` -- in-memory stand-in for the boto3 Table resource,\n  so the tests run without AWS. It follows DynamoDB's expression rules\n  (see its docstring).\n- `tests/test_feed.py` -- the tests.\n- `logs/` -- what came in this week: the production error on hide and a bug\n  report from staging.\n\nRun the tests (Python 3, no dependencies; on the servers `boto3` is\ninstalled and `STORIES_TABLE` names the table):\n\n    python3 -m unittest discover tests\ntotal 16\ndrwx------    8 valentinakoniukhova  wheel   256 Oct 20 20:29 .\ndrwxrwxrwt  240 root                 wheel  7680 Oct 20 20:29 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x   12 valentinakoniukhova  wheel   384 Oct 20 20:29 .git\n-rw-r--r--    1 valentinakoniukhova  wheel    13 Oct 20 20:29 .gitignore\n-rw-r--r--    1 valentinakoniukhova  wheel   819 Oct 20 20:29 README.md\ndrwxr-xr-x    4 valentinakoniukhova  wheel   128 Oct 20 20:29 logs\ndrwxr-xr-x    3 valentinakoniukhova  wheel    96 Oct 20 20:29 src\ndrwxr-xr-x    4 valentinakoniukhova  wheel   128 Oct 20 20:29 tests\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"The logs point to two separate DynamoDB expression issues: `hide()` writes `hidden` as a bare reserved name, while `feed()` projects `hidden` the same way, so its filtering step never sees the flag in the table stand-in. I’m adding aliases on both paths and tests that exercise the full hide-to-feed flow and a manually hidden row."}}
